  "status_text": "A rule about NOT gates came back checked: on graphs with no repeated rows or columns, if AND and OR gates alone cannot get under a certain size, adding NOT gates does not get under it either. Checked in Lean, on one-a-side inputs: for every n by m graph with n and m at least 2, no two equal rows and no two equal columns, if no fan-in-two AND/OR circuit has at most n + m - 3 gates, then every fan-in-two AND/OR/NOT circuit has at least n + m - 2 [L-meta-25016].",
